Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:51:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Complete the community endpoints the website integrates
 against

The NeverBeen website's community pages (companions, circles, journey feed,
message book, chats, notifications, gallery, followers/following, settings,
about me, devices, moderation) now read and write every dataset through this
API, and five gaps remained that left the website working against stale or
invented data:

* About me sub-sections: PUT /api/profile accepts aboutMeDetailsJson and
  ProfileDto answers it (Users.AboutMeDetailsJson), so the structured
  About-me editor (intro, work, education, hobbies, per-field visibility)
  survives a sign-in on another browser instead of living only in the
  website's localStorage.

* Presence: PUT /api/profile accepts activeStatus (validated against
  Active / Busy / Don't Disturb / Away / Inactive / Custom) and
  customStatusText; ProfileDto carries the stored columns, so the presence
  picker and the companions' online states come from the database.

* Cover photo: PUT/DELETE /api/profile/cover upload and remove
  Users.CoverPhotoData (validated like the profile photo) and
  GET /api/profile/{id}/cover serves it; ProfileDto.CoverPhotoUrl points at
  the stored bytes. The website could only keep cover photos as data URLs.

* Blue-tick verification: PUT /api/profile/settings persists isVerified,
  verificationEmail and verificationType onto the member row and mirrors
  them into the settings section, so verification survives a new browser.

* Journey tags: POST /api/journey and PUT /api/journey/{id} accept
  taggedCompanionIds - create adds them, update replaces the tag set - so a
  freshly created post carries its tagged companions without one POST per
  tag afterwards.

* Message book photographs: POST /api/messagebook accepts imageUrl and
  CommentDto answers it, so entries posted with a picture show it after a
  reload.

README documents the complete integration surface.
